  "log_sha256": "d7534ca542b5f4f1a9aa60d3607ddefda37fe27ed8ebdb11c4af5e82f13209ba",
  "notes": [
    "Final full suite includes strengthened tiny-row shape/length checks and near-positive/negative-f32MAX native f32 statistics cases.",
    "All five statistics methods load native low arrays directly; shared reduction planner/tree/final f32 fold only materialize bounded row partials and actual results.",
    "Tiny moment rows use exact integer power-of-two lifting; nonzero normalized BF16 subnormal results with minimum positive epsilon passed strict relative checks.",
    "Shared low-statistics conformance passed on the first GPU run without tolerance changes. A private nearly-zero mean check initially used relative-only tolerance; corrected to a coordinate-scale f32 error bound, with initial log retained.",
    "No MLX low-statistics performance measurement was made."
  ],
